      "value": "@{5c1475afb7ce126e9e0e3a39|full_name}: The hip would move directly away from the head to compensate for a crunched spine. There would be no backwards movement associated with the crunched spine. The current \"drift\" (I assume you're referring to the backwards movement of the hip) would be removed, but as a consequence avatars will have more knee bending (even without bending your knees IRL) every time the spine is crunched (which usually happens when looking down).\nI was unsure about implementing the backwards motion in the hip to compensate the knee bend, because the other two modes (lock hip, lock all) are already available to anyone who doesn't like knees bending at the wrong time. Because the backwards motion is receiving a negative reaction I'm considering removing it. The question to the community is would the knees bending every time your spine is compressed be better than the hip drifting to the back? (of course only referring to the \"lock head\" mode)",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
