      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{6161a61a2c0de966b4e43486|full_name}: I feel like part of it is the difference between sitting/standing regimes here. I already feel that head lock is inappropriate for standing, at least for my rig, and would prefer it for sitting, if not for the very visible knee and hip motion that occurs with the smallest head movements. Ultimately my preference is to reduce the knee motion when sitting, but I'll note that (as I mentioned in my other canny) there are some directions of motion (looking down) where i suspect distorting the spine would work better and others (looking up) where I suspect moving the hip would work better.",
      "viewerReactions": null
